232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 151 0 R
/T (Harold Cohen asks whether a system that evaluates, decides, and satisfies constraints is, in some limited sense, thinking.  I encountered this question most acutely in my final two projects, both of which transform quantitative data into something that feels inhabited.)
/E (Harold Cohen asks whether a system that evaluates, decides, and satisfies constraints is, in some limited sense, thinking.  I encountered this question most acutely in my final two projects, both of which transform quantitative data into something that feels inhabited.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
