242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 153 0 R
/T (This was the project where I felt the strongest shift from control toward collaboration. The system had to be tuned carefully, and a lot of the final form came from solving things that were not working: audio overlap, drawing order, video loading, and memory triggers. What surprised me most is that these technical problems were not separate from the concept; they actually helped me understand it better. In the end, the project felt less like a map of Shanghai Metro and more like a way of listening to what a city remembers but does not officially record.)
/E (This was the project where I felt the strongest shift from control toward collaboration. The system had to be tuned carefully, and a lot of the final form came from solving things that were not working: audio overlap, drawing order, video loading, and memory triggers. What surprised me most is that these technical problems were not separate from the concept; they actually helped me understand it better. In the end, the project felt less like a map of Shanghai Metro and more like a way of listening to what a city remembers but does not officially record.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
