674 0 obj
<<
/Title (Looking across six projects, I notice a pattern. I always began with a city and arrived somewhere more personal. The city is legible. You can map it, photograph it, date it. But what interested me was what it does not record: the feeling of walking the same campus in four different emotional states, the memory of an afternoon at a metro station that appears on no official map, the minute in which four lines of code briefly shared a canvas and produced something I did not plan. Code became the instrument for holding both the systemic and the intimate simultaneously. I did not set out to make personal work. I set out to make work about cities. But every time I built a system, I ended up putting something of my own inside it.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 761 0 R
/Next 569 0 R
>>
endobj
